"answer": "Rosacea can cause skin symptoms such as frequent facial redness or flushing, small red lines under the skin, acne, a swollen nose, and thick skin on the forehead, chin, and cheeks [MLP-1247]. Eye symptoms include red, dry, itchy eyes and sometimes vision problems [MLP-1247]. The provided materials do not list additional specific eye symptoms beyond these."
